section S_R_C5
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace Formalism.FourierDecayAlt.P.MAx3.R

open Finset

/- English proof (translation)
Rewrite using `[← prod_const, ← prod_mul_distrib]`. Use `prod_congr rfl fun i _ => by ring` and prove the remaining obligations.
-/
theorem prod_neg_flip (s : Finset ℕ) (c : ℕ → ℝ) (x : ℝ) :
    ∏ i ∈ s, (x - c i) = (-1) ^ s.card * ∏ i ∈ s, (c i - x) := by
  rw [← prod_const, ← prod_mul_distrib]
  refine prod_congr rfl fun i _ => by ring

/- English proof (translation)
Establish `hj'` using `mem_Icc.1 hj`. Establish `hmono : ∀ n, ∀ i, 1 ≤ i → i + n ≤ k → a i ≤ a (i + n)`. Introduce `n`. Proceed by induction on `n with`. Consider the case `zero => intro i _ _`.

Simplify using the standard rewrite rules. Consider the case `succ n ih`. Introduce `i hi hin`. Establish `h1` using `ih i hi (by omega)`. Establish `h2` using `hab (i + n) (by simp [mem_Icc]; omega)`.

Rewrite using `[show i + (n + 1) = i + n + 1 by ring]; linarith [h2.1, h2.2]`. Establish `hle : ∀ i i', 1 ≤ i → i ≤ i' → i' ≤ k → a i ≤ a i'` using `fun i i' h1 h2 h3 => by`. Use `hmono (i' - i) i h1 (by omega); rwa [Nat.add_sub_cancel' h2] at this` as an intermediate fact. Unfold `resA`. Rewrite using `[← prod_filter_mul_prod_filter_not (Icc 1 k) (fun i => i ≤ j), ← prod_filter_mul_prod_filter_not ((Icc 1 (k - 1)).erase j) (fun m => m < j)]`.

Use `set N1 := ∏ i ∈ (Icc 1 k).filter (fun i => i ≤ j), (b j - a i)`. Rewrite using `[prod_neg_flip ((Icc 1 k).filter (fun i => ¬ i ≤ j)) a (b j), prod_neg_flip (((Icc 1 (k - 1)).erase j).filter (fun m => ¬ m < j)) b (b j)]`. Establish `hc1 : ((Icc 1 k).filter (fun i => ¬ i ≤ j)).card = k - j`. Establish `: (Icc 1 k).filter (fun i => ¬ i ≤ j) = Ioc j k` using `by ext i; simp [mem_Ioc]; omega`. Rewrite using `[this, Nat.card_Ioc]`.

Establish `hc2 : (((Icc 1 (k - 1)).erase j).filter (fun m => ¬ m < j)).card = k - 1 - j`. Establish `: ((Icc 1 (k - 1)).erase j).filter (fun m => ¬ m < j) = Ioc j (k - 1)` using `by ext i; simp [mem_Ioc]; omega`. Rewrite using `[this, Nat.card_Ioc]`. Rewrite using `[hc1, hc2]`. Establish `hN1 : 0 ≤ N1` using `prod_nonneg fun i hi => by`.

